WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.840
Speaker 1: . Let's hear from some&nbsp;
people in the audience. We take calls&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:11.680
on the Friday show via discord at David Pakman&nbsp;
dot com slash Discord. Let's start today with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:15.920
Nevin from Tennessee. Nevin, welcome&nbsp;
to the show. What's on your mind today?&nbsp;

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:19.760
Speaker 2: Hey, David, I had to question&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:23.040
first of all.
Speaker 1: There's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:26.640
something there's something that just banged in&nbsp;
the background. You said you have to question.&nbsp;

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:35.280
Speaker 2: Yes. Yes. Okay. Okay. So firstly, do&nbsp;
you think that progressive economic reforms such&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:41.840
as universal healthcare, tuition forgiveness,&nbsp;
etc. can be accomplished without a big economic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:49.920
depression, such as for the New Deal during FDR.
Speaker 1: You said, can can we avoid an economic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:56.800
depression through programs like the New Deal?
Speaker 2: Yes. Like universal health care&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:00.960
or news programs? Like stuff like that.
Speaker 1: Yeah. I mean, generally speaking,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:08.960
government spending that is carefully thought,&nbsp;
carefully conceived to be economically stimulative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:15.120
through what we call demand side stimulus is a&nbsp;
good way to both do good things for the people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:21.200
and also to help the economy. The devil is in&nbsp;
the details of the programs and the spending.&nbsp;

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:29.680
Speaker 2: Well, okay. And I'd also like&nbsp;
to ask you, what can liberals like myself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:32.960
do in our house?
Speaker 1:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:36.480
Did you say for the progressive cause?
Speaker 2: Yes.&nbsp;

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:43.040
Speaker 1: Well, get involved in local races at&nbsp;
some level, even in southern red states. Is there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:49.040
an opportunity to replace a right wing state rep&nbsp;
or state senator with someone more progressive? Is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:53.840
there an opportunity to get involved in a school&nbsp;
board? There's lots of local opportunities and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:57.760
also you can still phone bank for any race&nbsp;
across the country that you want. So like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:04.480
imagine that you're in Alabama and there's no&nbsp;
likely Democratic Senate challenger in Alabama.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:08.880
You can phone bank for Fetterman in Pennsylvania.&nbsp;
Right, or you can whatever. So there's there's no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:12.960
shortage of ways to get involved.
Speaker 2:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:17.120
Yeah. That's all. Thanks for taking my call.
Speaker 1: Nevin, I have to ask, where are you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:21.840
calling from? The noise in the background is wild.
Speaker 2: I'm on a bus ride.&nbsp;

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:24.880
Speaker 1: Oh, you're on a bus right now?
Speaker 2: Yeah.&nbsp;

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:27.760
Speaker 1: Do people around, you&nbsp;
know you're on The David Pakman Show.&nbsp;

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:32.240
Speaker 2: They probably don't know what it is.
Speaker 1: They don't know. All right,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:36.240
Evan, thank you for the call.
Speaker 2: You're welcome. All right.&nbsp;

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.800
Speaker 1: Nevin Nevin from&nbsp;
thank you, Nevin from a bus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:45.120
in Tennessee. That is something else. I don't know&nbsp;
that we've ever had a call from a bus necessarily.

